; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Arcade Sound Effects
; CATEGORY: Music & Sound
; LEVEL:    Beginner
; TAGS:     sound, effects, for loop, games
; SUMMARY:  Builds a siren, a laser, a coin pickup, a power-up and a falling bomb out of nothing but short beeps.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   Old video games had no recorded sounds. Every zap and ding was
;   made from quick beeps whose pitch went up or down. This program
;   plays five classic effects one after another and writes the name
;   of each one on the screen while you hear it.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run with the sound on. Then type the name of one effect in
;   the command center, for example:  laser   or   siren 5
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * a sweep is many very short notes with the pitch changing a bit each time
;   * FOR [f 300 1200 40] counts from 300 to 1200 in steps of 40
;   * a negative step counts downward
;   * RUN carries out a list of instructions kept in a variable
;   * small procedures with good names can be reused in games
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Make the laser longer by making the step smaller (try -20).
;   * Invent a "jump" sound: a quick sweep up, then a quick sweep down.
;   * Put COIN inside one of your own game programs.
; ============================================================

; A police siren goes up and down, up and down.
to siren :times
  repeat :times [
    for [f 600 1000 25] [tone :f 12]
    for [f 1000 600 -25] [tone :f 12]
  ]
end

; A laser drops quickly from very high to low.
to laser
  for [f 2000 300 -100] [tone :f 10]
end

; A coin is two bright notes, the second one higher and longer.
to coin
  tone 988 70
  tone 1319 300
end

; A power-up climbs in little jumps, each jump ending a bit higher.
to powerup
  for [base 300 700 100] [
    for [f :base :base + 300 60] [tone :f 15]
  ]
end

; The bomb whistles down, then explodes in a burst of random noise.
to bomb
  for [f 1500 400 -10] [tone :f 15]
  repeat 40 [tone 60 + random 120 8]
end

; Write the name of an effect big on the screen, then play it.
; The input is a list of instructions such as [siren 4]; its first
; word is the name, and RUN carries out the whole list.
to show.effect :effect :c
  clean
  setpencolor :c
  penup setxy -150 0 pendown
  label first :effect
  run :effect
  wait 30
end

clearscreen
hideturtle
setbackground 0
setlabelheight 60
show.effect [siren 4] 4
show.effect [laser] 2
show.effect [coin] 6
show.effect [powerup] 3
show.effect [bomb] 14
clean
setpencolor 7
penup setxy -260 0 pendown
setlabelheight 30
label [Type laser, coin, powerup, bomb or siren 3]
